# An unknown array method is rejected

Verifies a method name that is not a built-in array end operation is
rejected, and that the diagnostic lists the supported method names.

>>> source
let values: int[] = [1]
values->length()

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: an array has no method `length`; the supported methods are push, append, pop, unshift, prepend, shift at Span { start: 24, end: 40 }

<<< exit
1
